==Faroese==

===Etymology===
From the {{etyl|non|fo}} {{term|matr||food|lang=non}} from the {{etyl|gem-pro|fo}} {{recons|matiz|lang=gem-pro}}. Whence also Old English {{term|mete|mēte|lang=ang}} (Middle English {{term|mete|mēte|lang=enm}} from which English {{term|meat|lang=en}} came); Gothic {{term|mats|lang=got}}; Old High German {{term|maz|lang=goh}}, Swedish {{term|mat|lang=sv}}, Danish {{term|mad|lang=da}} and Icelandic {{term|matur|lang=is}}.

===Noun===
{{fo-noun|m|matar|-}}

# [[meal]], [[food]]

====Declension====
{{fo-decl-noun-m12-s|mat}}

[[Category:fo:Food and drink]]

