==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From the {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|matr||food|lang=non}} from the {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|matiz|lang=gem-pro}}. Whence also Old English {{term|mete|mēte|lang=ang}} (Middle English {{term|mete|mēte|lang=enm}} from which English {{term|meat|lang=en}} came); Gothic {{term|𐌼𐌰𐍄𐍃|sc=Goth|tr=mats|lang=got}}; Old High German {{term|maz|lang=goh}}, Swedish {{term|mat|lang=sv}}, Danish {{term|mad|lang=da}} and Faroese {{term|matur|lang=fo}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈmaːtʏr/|lang=is}} ({{audio|is-matur.ogg|listen}})
*: {{rhymes|aːtʏr|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|m|matar|matar}}<ref>http://bin.arnastofnun.is/leit.php?q=matur</ref>

# [[food]]
#: ''Þetta var staðgóður '''matur'''.''
#:: This was a hearty '''meal'''.
#: ''Hvað er í '''matinn'''?''
#:: What's for '''dinner'''?

====Declension====
{{is-decl-noun-m-s1|m|a|t|ur|ar=ar}}

